B.a4R=s(["Switch media families without rebuilding your search.","Use examples and focused result tabs when the right words are still hiding.","Stay close to the source: every result leads back to Commons."],t.s)
B.au4=new A.kh("01","START WITH THE OPEN WEB","The world\u2019s largest visual archive. One clear starting point.","CommonsLens searches Wikimedia Commons across images, audio, video, documents, vectors, and 3D. Type the thing you want, or the thing you almost remember, and let the archive meet you halfway.",B.a4R,"assets/features_media/glacier_point.jpg","Glacier Point at Sunset, Yosemite NP, CA, US","Diliff \xb7 Own work \xb7 CC BY-SA 3.0 \xb7 Wikimedia Commons","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glacier_Point_at_Sunset,_Yosemite_NP,_CA,_US_-_Diliff.jpg",B.fo,"DISCOVERY ENGINE",B.c8,"Start exploring","search","/",!0)
B.a52=s(["Instant choices update the result set as you make them.","Technical filters find files that fit the job, not just the topic.","Keep rights and attribution in view before you fall in love with a file."],t.s)
B.SD=new A.t(1,0.7098039215686275,0.8117647058823529,0.5411764705882353,B.e)
B.au7=new A.kh("02","FOLLOW THE THREAD","Precision without the paperwork.","A good filter should sharpen the picture, not bury the idea. Combine subjects, categories, templates, rights, quality, dates, dimensions, file size, metadata, and location while your search keeps taking shape.",B.a52,"assets/features_media/midtown_manhattan.jpg","Midtown Manhattan from Weehawken, September 2021","King of Hearts \xb7 Own work \xb7 CC BY-SA 4.0 \xb7 Wikimedia Commons","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_HDR.jpg",B.yA,"FILTER SYSTEM",B.SD,"See the filters","advanced-filters",null,!0)
B.a3W=s(["Use nearby coordinates to turn a place into a search.","Move between map and grid when context or comparison matters.","Let geography surface the unexpected."],t.s)
B.Sb=new A.t(1,0.8941176470588236,0.6392156862745098,0.4235294117647059,B.e)
B.au3=new A.kh("03","A TIME AND PLACE FOR EVERYTHING","Search by where the story happened.","Some media only makes sense when you know where it belongs. Put a point on the map, set a radius, or explore geographic context, then move from place to file without losing the thread.",B.a3W,"assets/features_media/iss_aug2005.jpg","ISS, August 2005","NASA \xb7 Public domain \xb7 Wikimedia Commons","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS_Aug2005.jpg",B.yy,"GEOGRAPHIC CONTEXT",B.Sb,"Open the map","map","/map",!0)
B.a5p=s(["See dimensions, dates, creators, categories, and structured statements together.","Trace a promising file back to its Commons source.","Make the reuse decision with evidence, not a guess."],t.s)
B.Yp=new A.a6(61103,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.S_=new A.t(1,0.8156862745098039,0.6078431372549019,0.9098039215686274,B.e)
B.au5=new A.kh("04","LOOK CLOSER","An image is not the whole file.","Open an asset and get the context that makes it usable: metadata, structured data, related media, source links, reported rights, and a ready-to-edit attribution starting point.",B.a5p,"assets/features_media/monet_bridge.jpg","Claude Monet: Le Pont d'Argenteuil","Pierre Andr\xe9 Leclercq \xb7 Public domain \xb7 Wikimedia Commons","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Claude_Monet.-_Le_Pont_d'Argenteuil.JPG",B.Yp,"CONTEXT & RIGHTS",B.S_,"Learn about reuse","reuse",null,!0)
B.a3a=s(["Build local collections of references without copying the Commons catalogue.","Securely download media separately from CSV metadata and URLs.","Explore an uploader\u2019s portfolio when one good file opens a larger trail."],t.s)
B.SP=new A.t(1,0.9411764705882353,0.7764705882352941,0.42745098039215684,B.e)
B.au2=new A.kh("05","MAKE IT YOURS","Collect discoveries before they disappear.","The best research rarely arrives in one sitting. Bookmark files, arrange them in folders, download what you need, and export the metadata that lets your work travel.",B.a3a,"assets/features_media/jaws_of_death.jpg","Into the Jaws of Death","CPHoM Robert F. Sargent \xb7 Public domain \xb7 Wikimedia Commons","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Into_the_Jaws_of_Death_23-0455M_edit.jpg",B.lY,"COLLECTIONS & EXPORT",B.SP,"See saved work","bookmarks","/bookmarks",!0)
B.a2O=s(["Keep each step visible instead of hiding the method in a tangle of tabs.","Reuse a workflow when the question grows from one file to a collection.","Export the result when it is ready for the next tool."],t.s)
B.SW=new A.t(1,0.5176470588235295,0.8274509803921568,0.796078431372549,B.e)
B.au6=new A.kh("06","BUILD WORKFLOWS","Build a visual pipeline","Pipelines connect fetching, filtering, enrichment, and export into a visual workflow. Start with a question; come back later with a process you can inspect, change, and run again.",B.a2O,"assets/features_media/dna_orbit.gif","DNA Orbit Animated Clean","Circli \xb7 Own work \xb7 CC BY-SA 4.0 \xb7 Wikimedia Commons","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DNA_Orbit_Animated_Clean.gif",B.hH,"REPEATABLE WORKFLOWS",B.SW,"Build a pipeline","pipelines","/pipeline",!1)
